.TH FREECAD\-MCP 1 "August 2026" "freecad-mcp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
freecad-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for FreeCAD integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B freecad-mcp
[\fB\-\-only\-text\-feedback\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR \fIADDRESS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B freecad-mcp
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that enables LLM-based coding agents to
interact with FreeCAD for 3D modelling and related tasks. It connects to the
FreeCAD MCP addon running inside a FreeCAD instance via an RPC server, exposing
tools for document management, object creation and editing, code execution, parts
library access, view screenshots, and finite element analysis.
.PP
The server communicates with clients over stdio using the JSON-RPC based MCP
protocol, making it compatible with any MCP-compatible client such as Claude Desktop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-only\-text\-feedback
Disable screenshot feedback from all tools. When set, tools that normally return
both text and image content will return only text. This reduces token usage when
visual feedback is not needed. Individual tools may also accept an
.B include_screenshot
parameter for per-call control; however, this flag always takes precedence and
suppresses all images globally.
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIADDRESS\fR
The hostname or IP address of the FreeCAD RPC server to connect to. Defaults to
.IR localhost .
The value must be a valid IPv4/IPv6 address or hostname. Use this option when
FreeCAD is running on a remote machine.
.SH EXAMPLES
Connect to a FreeCAD instance running on a remote host via IPv6, suppressing image feedback:
.PP
.nf
\fBfreecad-mcp \-\-host fd00::42 \-\-only\-text\-feedback\fR
.fi
.SH CONFIGURATION
The MCP server is typically invoked by an MCP client. A minimal Claude Desktop
configuration in
.IR claude_desktop_config.json :
.PP
.nf
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "freecad": {
      "command": "freecad-mcp"
    }
  }
}
.fi
.SH PREREQUISITES
Before running
.B freecad-mcp,
the FreeCAD MCP addon must be installed and the RPC server started within FreeCAD.
The addon provides a workbench with a
.B Start RPC Server
command in the
.B FreeCAD MCP
toolbar. Auto-start can be enabled from the
.B FreeCAD MCP
menu so the RPC server starts automatically on each FreeCAD launch.
.PP
The RPC server listens on port 9875 by default.
.SH MCP TOOLS
The available tools can be queried from the server using JSON-RPC over stdio. The MCP protocol requires an initialization handshake first:
.PP
.nf
\fBprintf '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"test","version":"0.1"}}}\\n{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"notifications/initialized"}\\n{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/list","params":{}}' | \\\e
    freecad-mcp 2>/dev/null | jq -r 'select(.result.tools) | .result.tools[].name'\fR
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
This tool does not read any environment variables directly. Configuration is passed
via command-line arguments by the MCP client.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcp (1),
.BR freecad (1)
